  "worked_solution": "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}-{e}^{x-2} & >\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -{e}^{x-2} & >\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ {e}^{x-2} & <-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause a power of a positive number is always greater than $0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{e}^{x-2}>0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality ${e}^{x-2}<-\\frac{3}{5}$ has no solutions.",
